</li>
<li class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-race">
<span class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-date">June 2027</span>
<h3 class="lsu-scope-world-series">Australia<span class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-cobrand">x DCG</span>
</h3>
</li>
</ul>
<div class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-rules">
<details class="lsu-scope-world-series">
<summary class="lsu-scope-world-series">
<span class="lsu-scope-world-series">
<strong class="lsu-scope-world-series">Tied on loops?</strong>
<small class="lsu-scope-world-series">Ties at both qualification cutoffs count.</small>
</span>
<span class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-rule-copy">
<p class="lsu-scope-world-series">Everyone with the same completed-loop count as 15th overall qualifies. The same applies to everyone tied with the 5th woman.</p>
<p class="lsu-scope-world-series">These two cutoffs are applied separately in each qualifying race.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="lsu-scope-world-series">
<summary class="lsu-scope-world-series">
<span class="lsu-scope-world-series">
<strong class="lsu-scope-world-series">One athlete. One place.</strong>
<small class="lsu-scope-world-series">Duplicate qualifications do not roll down.</small>
</span>
<span class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-rule-copy">
<p class="lsu-scope-world-series">Qualify through more than one race, or through both the overall and women’s standings, and you receive one Finals place.</p>
<p class="lsu-scope-world-series">A duplicate place is not passed to the next ranked athlete. The tie rule still applies.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>
<p class="lsu-scope-world-series ws-future">Additional qualification opportunities may be announced.</p>
</section>
